```cs
private static readonly Regex CommentMatch = new Regex(@"(?<=@@@\s).*", RegexOptions.Compiled);

[PexMethod]
public void PUT_CountContract([PexAssumeUnderTest]ArrayList arrList)
{
    AssumePrecondition.IsTrue(true);

    var arrListCopy = new ArrayList(arrList);

    int New_Ret = arrList.Count;

    arrListCopy.Add(10000);
    int New_arrListCountAfterAdd = arrList.Count;

    PexObserve.ValueForViewing("$New_ret", New_Ret);
    PexObserve.ValueForViewing("$New_arrListCountAfterAdd", New_arrListCountAfterAdd);

    // @@@ If the return value is negative, arrListCopy size is not -1
    Debug.Assert(New_Ret >= 0 || New_arrListCountAfterAdd != -1, CommentMatch.Match(new StackTrace().GetFrame(0).GetMethod().GetCustomAttribute<PexMethodAttribute>().Comment).Value);
}

```

This code first extracts the comment for the PUT_CountContract method and then uses it in a Debug.Assert statement. The regular expression used is "\(?<=@@@\\s).*" to match any text that is preceded by "@@@ " (including a space), meaning that the comment must be immediately after the "@@@" mark. The `StackTrace().GetFrame(0)` is used to get the stack frame where the method was called, and `GetMethod().GetCustomAttribute<PexMethodAttribute>().Comment` is used to get the comment of the method (if any).

